  cites Game chapter Color

 A render target can be pointed at a rectangle INSIDE a larger panel, by
 offsetting its base address while keeping the panel's own stride. That is
 what keeps a desktop's sidebar and taskbar on the glass around a moving
 3D view, and the risk is the whole of it: get it wrong by one and the
 scene shears across the chrome, which on real hardware looks like a
 corrupt display rather than a wrong number.

 The subject here is `r3d-target-at`, not GopScene. GopScene reached the
 pane this way until 2026-07-30 and now renders into a back buffer and
 blits, so its own path is covered by `gop-scene-backbuffer` and this file
 covers the primitive underneath both.

 So this renders into a scratch panel pre-filled with a sentinel and
 asks where the pixels landed. The sidebar columns and the taskbar rows
 must still hold the sentinel and the content pane must not, on the same
 frame. Checking only that the content changed would pass just as well
 with a renderer that painted the entire panel.

 The orbit is checked too. Cordic is used rather than Matrix4's
 mat4-sin-approx because that one is a two-term Taylor: at half a turn
 it answers -2.03 where the sine is 0, so a camera driven by it would
 leave the scene entirely. Two positions half a turn apart must put the
 eye on opposite sides of the origin, which is what an approximation
 that has passed its turning point cannot do.

 We say:

Section: Panel

  pw : Integer = 320
  ph : Integer = 240
  sidebar : Integer = 160
  taskbar : Integer = 24
  sentinel : Integer = 12648430

  sky : Integer
  sky = rgb-to-packed (rgb 20 20 30)

Section: Scene

  scene-camera : Integer -> Camera3D
  scene-camera (angle) =
    let ca = real-from-int (cordic-cos angle)
    in let sa = real-from-int (cordic-sin angle)
    in camera3d-new (vec3-new (ca * 5.2) 2200.0 (sa * 5.2)) (vec3-new 0.0 300.0 0.0) 0.785

  build-scene : Integer -> Scene3DState
  build-scene (dummy) =
    let scene = scene3d-new (scene-camera 0)
    in let ground = sn3-with-mesh "ground" (mesh-plane 3000 3000) (emat-flat (rgb 90 80 62))
    in let cube = sn3-set-pos (sn3-with-mesh "cube" (mesh-cube 900) (emat-shiny (rgb 90 130 210) 32)) (-900.0) 450.0 0.0
    in let s2 = scene3d-add (scene3d-add scene ground) cube
    in let key = dir-light (vec3-new (-400.0) 800.0 400.0) (rgb 255 250 235) 850
    in scene3d-set-ambient (scene3d-add-light s2 key) 260

Section: Counting

  fill-panel : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  fill-panel (base) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else let d = poke-32 base (i * 4) sentinel
    in fill-panel base (i + 1) n

 Counts sentinel pixels inside an arbitrary rectangle of the panel, so
 the same helper can ask about the sidebar, the taskbar and the content.

  count-rows : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-rows (base) (x0) (y0) (rw) (rh) (y) (acc) (dummy) =
    if y >= rh then acc
    else count-rows base x0 y0 rw rh (y + 1) (count-cols base x0 y0 rw y 0 acc) 0

  count-cols : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  count-cols (base) (x0) (y0) (rw) (y) (x) (acc) =
    if x >= rw then acc
    else if peek-32 base (((y0 + y) * pw + x0 + x) * 4) == sentinel then count-cols base x0 y0 rw y (x + 1) (acc + 1)
    else count-cols base x0 y0 rw y (x + 1) acc

  intact : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  intact (base) (x0) (y0) (rw) (rh) =
    count-rows base x0 y0 rw rh 0 0 0 == rw * rh

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let panel = alloc-bytes (pw * ph * 4)
    in let f = fill-panel panel 0 (pw * ph)
    in let cw = pw - sidebar
    in let ch = ph - taskbar
    in let tgt = r3d-target-at (panel + sidebar * 4) pw cw ch sky
    in let scene = build-scene 0
    in let d = r3d-render-into tgt scene
    in let side-ok = intact panel 0 0 sidebar ph
    in let task-ok = intact panel sidebar ch cw taskbar
    in let content-kept = count-rows panel sidebar 0 cw ch 0 0 0
    in let near = scene-camera 0
    in let far = scene-camera 3142
    in act
      print-line-uni ("sidebar untouched      : " & yn side-ok)
      print-line-uni ("taskbar untouched      : " & yn task-ok)
      print-line-uni ("content pane painted   : " & yn (content-kept == 0))
      print-line-uni ("orbit crosses origin   : " & yn (near.c3-eye.vx > 0.0 & far.c3-eye.vx < 0.0))
    end
  end

